/-
# Conjugacy classes of p-elements with p-element quotients (Kourovka Notebook Problem 5.32)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 5.32 (V. D. Mazurov): let p be a prime, C a
conjugacy class of p-elements of a finite group G, and suppose that for any two elements x and y of
C the product xy⁻¹ is a p-element; is the subgroup generated by C a p-group?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.PGroup

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.ConjugacyClassPElementsPGroupKourovka5Problem32Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 5.32 (V. D.
Mazurov). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700315 (`KOU-5.32`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

A `p`-element is an element of order a power of `p`; `C` is the conjugacy class of `x`.
-/

/-- Kourovka 5.32 (V. D. Mazurov): let `p` be a prime and `C` the conjugacy class of a
`p`-element `x` of a finite group `G` such that `y z⁻¹` is a `p`-element for all `y, z ∈ C`. Then
the subgroup generated by `C` is a `p`-group. -/
def conjugacyClassPElementsGeneratesPGroup : Prop :=
  ∀ (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] (G : Type) [Group G] [Finite G] (x : G), (∃ k, orderOf x = p ^ k) →
    (∀ y z : G, IsConj x y → IsConj x z → ∃ k, orderOf (y * z⁻¹) = p ^ k) →
      IsPGroup p (Subgroup.closure {y | IsConj x y})

/--
Resolved true: the Kourovka Archive answers 5.32 "Yes, it is", by Xiao for `p > 2` (Sci. in China 34
(1991), 1025-1031) and by Zenkov for `p = 2` (Proc. IIIrd Int. Conf. on Algebra, Krasnoyarsk 1993,
de Gruyter 1996, 297-302). Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in
Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved
Problems, Problem 5.32 (V. D. Mazurov); resolution: W. Xiao, Sci. in China 34 (1991), no. 9,
1025-1031 (p > 2); V. I. Zenkov, in: Algebra. Proc. IIIrd Int. Conf. on Algebra, Krasnoyarsk, 1993,
de Gruyter, Berlin, 1996, 297-302 (p = 2), Kourovka Archive, Problem 5.32: Yes, it is (Xiao for p >
2; Zenkov for p = 2), https://arxiv.org/abs/1401.0300v49.
-/
public theorem_wanted conjugacyClassPElementsGeneratesPGroup_holds :
    conjugacyClassPElementsGeneratesPGroup

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.ConjugacyClassPElementsPGroupKourovka5Problem32Wanted
